IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lpul-dates`
IMPORT `lpul-client`

-- Legal Profession Uniform Law (Victoria) -- worked cases for the client's questions (lpul-client.l4) and the date
-- helpers. Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's output.
-- Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. The facts are illustrative.
-- Weekdays used: 1 July 2026 is a Wednesday, 3 July a Friday, 6 July a Monday; 30 October 2026 is a Friday and
-- 3 November 2026 (Melbourne Cup day) a Tuesday.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`
`individual` MEANS `an individual, or another client not listed in s 170(2)`
`government` MEANS `a government authority in Australia or in a foreign country`
`instructed` MEANS `d` 1 3 2026
`claim` MEANS `another matter (for example a personal injury or compensation claim)`
`no holidays` MEANS LIST `d` 31 12 2099

§§ `Dates`

#ASSERT `the weekday of` (`d` 1 7 2026) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `the weekday of` (`d` 3 7 2026) EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `the weekday of` (`d` 4 7 2026) EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `the weekday of` (`d` 5 7 2026) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the weekday of` (`d` 3 11 2026) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the same day` 12 `months after` (`d` 29 2 2028) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2029
#ASSERT `the same day` 6 `months after` (`d` 31 8 2025) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2026
#ASSERT `the same day` 4 `months after` (`d` 30 6 2026) EQUALS `d` 30 10 2026
#ASSERT `the date` 60 `days after` (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS `d` 30 9 2026
#ASSERT NOT (`is a business day` (`d` 4 7 2026) `given the holidays` `no holidays`)
#ASSERT NOT (`is a business day` (`d` 3 11 2026) `given the holidays` (LIST `d` 3 11 2026))
#ASSERT `is a business day` (`d` 3 11 2026) `given the holidays` `no holidays`

§§ `s 170, Sch 4 cl 18 -- who Part 4.3 protects`

-- First instructed on the commencement day: covered; the day before: the old legislation (cl 18(1)).
#ASSERT `Does Part 4.3 protect me` `individual` (`d` 1 7 2015) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does Part 4.3 protect me` `individual` (`d` 30 6 2015) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does Part 4.3 protect me` `government` `instructed` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does Part 4.3 protect me` `a law practice` `instructed` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does Part 4.3 protect me` `a person who agreed to pay costs on a basis resulting from a tender process` `instructed` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I require a negotiated costs agreement` `individual` `instructed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I require a negotiated costs agreement` `a body or person incorporated outside Australia` `instructed` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 174 -- disclosure at the start`

#ASSERT `What disclosure must I be given at the start` `individual` `instructed` 750 FALSE EQUALS `none is required: the total legal costs are not likely to exceed the lower threshold of $750, though the law practice may give me the uniform standard disclosure form (s 174(4))`
#ASSERT `What disclosure must I be given at the start` `individual` `instructed` 751 FALSE EQUALS `the uniform standard disclosure form, or full written disclosure: the total legal costs are not likely to exceed the higher threshold of $3000 (s 174(5), (6))`
#ASSERT `What disclosure must I be given at the start` `individual` `instructed` 3000 FALSE EQUALS `the uniform standard disclosure form, or full written disclosure: the total legal costs are not likely to exceed the higher threshold of $3000 (s 174(5), (6))`
#ASSERT `What disclosure must I be given at the start` `individual` `instructed` 3001 FALSE EQUALS `full written disclosure of the basis of the costs, an estimate of the total costs, and my rights, when or as soon as practicable after I first instruct (s 174(1)(a), (2)(a), (6))`
#ASSERT `What disclosure must I be given at the start` `individual` `instructed` 50000 TRUE EQUALS `none from this law practice: it was retained for me by another law practice, which must disclose this practice's costs to me as well as its own (s 175)`
#ASSERT `What disclosure must I be given at the start` `government` `instructed` 50000 FALSE EQUALS `not covered: Part 4.3 does not protect me (s 170, Sch 4 cl 18)`

#ASSERT `Did my full disclosure meet s 174` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Did my full disclosure meet s 174` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Did my full disclosure meet s 174` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Did my full disclosure meet s 174` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Did my full disclosure meet s 174` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)

§§ `s 174(1)(b), (7), (8) -- further disclosure`

`nothing given` MEANS `no disclosure, because the costs were not likely to exceed $750`
`form given` MEANS `the uniform standard disclosure form`
`full given` MEANS `full disclosure under s 174(1)`
#ASSERT `Must I be given further disclosure` `individual` `instructed` `nothing given` 750 FALSE EQUALS `no: s 174 requires no further disclosure on these facts`
#ASSERT `Must I be given further disclosure` `individual` `instructed` `nothing given` 751 FALSE EQUALS `yes: I must be told in writing that the costs are now likely to exceed $750, and be given the uniform standard disclosure form or full disclosure (s 174(7))`
#ASSERT `Must I be given further disclosure` `individual` `instructed` `nothing given` 3001 FALSE EQUALS `yes: I must be told in writing that the costs are now likely to exceed $750, and be given full disclosure (s 174(7))`
#ASSERT `Must I be given further disclosure` `individual` `instructed` `form given` 3000 TRUE EQUALS `no: s 174 requires no further disclosure on these facts`
#ASSERT `Must I be given further disclosure` `individual` `instructed` `form given` 3001 FALSE EQUALS `yes: I must be told in writing that the costs are now likely to exceed $3000, and be given full disclosure (s 174(8))`
#ASSERT `Must I be given further disclosure` `individual` `instructed` `full given` 90000 TRUE EQUALS `yes: I must be told in writing of the significant change, with enough about its impact on my costs to decide how to go on (s 174(1)(b), (2)(b), (6))`
#ASSERT `Must I be given further disclosure` `individual` `instructed` `full given` 90000 FALSE EQUALS `no: s 174 requires no further disclosure on these facts`
#ASSERT `Must I be given further disclosure` `government` `instructed` `nothing given` 5000 FALSE EQUALS `not covered: Part 4.3 does not protect me (s 170, Sch 4 cl 18)`

§§ `s 177 -- before a settlement is executed`

`met` MEANS `met: both estimates were disclosed to me before the settlement was executed (s 177(1))`
`not met` MEANS `not met: both estimates were not disclosed to me before the settlement was executed, a contravention of the disclosure obligations (ss 177(1), 178)`
-- The day before execution: met. The same day, before execution: met; after: not met. The day after: not met.
#ASSERT `Was I given the settlement estimates in time` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE (`d` 9 8 2026) (`d` 10 8 2026) FALSE EQUALS `met`
#ASSERT `Was I given the settlement estimates in time` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE (`d` 10 8 2026) (`d` 10 8 2026) TRUE EQUALS `met`
#ASSERT `Was I given the settlement estimates in time` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE (`d` 10 8 2026) (`d` 10 8 2026) FALSE EQUALS `not met`
#ASSERT `Was I given the settlement estimates in time` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE (`d` 11 8 2026) (`d` 10 8 2026) FALSE EQUALS `not met`
#ASSERT `Was I given the settlement estimates in time` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 6 2026) (`d` 10 8 2026) FALSE EQUALS `met`
-- Only one estimate given: not met, whatever the day.
#ASSERT `Was I given the settlement estimates in time` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 6 2026) (`d` 10 8 2026) FALSE EQUALS `not met`
#ASSERT `Was I given the settlement estimates in time` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 6 2026) (`d` 10 8 2026) FALSE EQUALS `s 177 does not apply: my law practice is not negotiating the settlement of a litigious matter for me`
#ASSERT `Was I given the settlement estimates in time` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 6 2026) (`d` 10 8 2026) FALSE EQUALS `s 177 does not apply: my law practice is not negotiating the settlement of a litigious matter for me`
#ASSERT `Was I given the settlement estimates in time` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 6 2026) (`d` 10 8 2026) FALSE EQUALS `s 177 does not apply to this law practice: the law practice that retained it for me made the disclosure before the settlement was executed (s 177(2))`

§§ `s 178 -- failure to disclose`

#ASSERT `What follows from the failure to disclose to me` `individual` `instructed` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `my costs agreement (if any) is void, and I need not pay the legal costs until they have been assessed or a costs dispute about them has been determined; the law practice cannot sue me for them until then (s 178(1))`
#ASSERT `What follows from the failure to disclose to me` `individual` `instructed` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `nothing under s 178 for me: the disclosure was made to me, and only the other of client and third party payer missed out (s 178(2))`
#ASSERT `What follows from the failure to disclose to me` `individual` `instructed` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `nothing under s 178: it has been found that the law practice took reasonable steps, fixed the failure within 14 days, and the failure made no difference (s 178(3), Uniform Rules r 72A)`
#ASSERT `What follows from the failure to disclose to me` `individual` `instructed` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `nothing under s 178: the law practice did not contravene the disclosure obligations on these facts`
#ASSERT `What follows from the failure to disclose to me` `government` `instructed` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered: Part 4.3 does not protect me (s 170, Sch 4 cl 18)`

§§ `ss 178, 180-185 -- conditional costs agreements`

-- The arguments after kind of client, day, kind of matter: written, success, signed, advice statement, cooling-off days,
-- excludes assessment, uplift, litigious, reasonable belief, uplift percent, uplift basis, contingency, fixed costs,
-- disclosure broken.
`valid` MEANS `valid on these facts: none of the defects in ss 178, 180-183 applies`
#ASSERT `Is my conditional costs agreement valid` `individual` `instructed` `claim` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 25 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `valid`
#ASSERT `Is my conditional costs agreement valid` `individual` `instructed` `claim` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 25.01 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `void: its uplift fee is more than 25% of the legal costs otherwise payable in a litigious matter (ss 182(2)(b), 185(1)); the uplift fee cannot be recovered (s 185(3))`
-- Outside a litigious matter s 182(2) sets no cap and asks no belief in success.
#ASSERT `Is my conditional costs agreement valid` `individual` `instructed` `claim` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 40 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `valid`
#ASSERT `Is my conditional costs agreement valid` `individual` `instructed` `claim` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE 10 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `void: it provides for an uplift fee in a litigious matter without the law practice reasonably believing success reasonably likely (ss 182(2)(a), 185(1)); the uplift fee cannot be recovered (s 185(3))`
#ASSERT `Is my conditional costs agreement valid` `individual` `instructed` `claim` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 10 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `void: it does not state the basis of the uplift fee and an estimate, or a range of estimates with the major variables (ss 182(3), 185(1)); the uplift fee cannot be recovered (s 185(3))`
#ASSERT `Is my conditional costs agreement valid` `individual` `instructed` `claim` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 4 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `void: its cooling-off period is shorter than 5 clear business days (ss 181(4), 185(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my conditional costs agreement valid` `individual` `instructed` `claim` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 5 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `void: it is not in writing and in plain language, or does not set out what counts as a successful outcome (ss 181(2), 185(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my conditional costs agreement valid` `individual` `instructed` `claim` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 5 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `void: it is not signed by me, or does not state that I was told of my right to independent legal advice (ss 181(3), 185(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my conditional costs agreement valid` `individual` `instructed` `claim` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `void: it purports to exclude the costs from costs assessment (ss 180(4), 185(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my conditional costs agreement valid` `individual` `instructed` `claim` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 0 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `void: it is a prohibited contingency fee, calculated by reference to the amount recovered (ss 183, 185(1)); the law practice can recover nothing for its services in the matter (s 185(4))`
#ASSERT `Is my conditional costs agreement valid` `individual` `instructed` `claim` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 0 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `valid`
#ASSERT `Is my conditional costs agreement valid` `individual` `instructed` `claim` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `void: the law practice broke its costs disclosure obligations (s 178(1)(a))`
#ASSERT `Is my conditional costs agreement valid` `individual` `instructed` `proceedings under the Family Law Act 1975 (Cth)` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `void: a conditional costs agreement cannot be made in this kind of matter (ss 181(7), 185(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my conditional costs agreement valid` `individual` `instructed` `criminal proceedings` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `void: a conditional costs agreement cannot be made in this kind of matter (ss 181(7), 185(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my conditional costs agreement valid` `government` `instructed` `claim` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered: Part 4.3 does not protect me (s 170); ss 181(7), 182, 183 and 185(3)-(5) still apply to a commercial or government client`

