§§ `ss 196-198, Vic s 99(9) -- costs assessment`

`no dispute` MEANS `there has been no costs dispute about these costs`
-- Bill 15 March 2026: the last day is 15 March 2027.
#ASSERT `Can I have my costs assessed` `individual` `instructed` `the client` TRUE `no dispute` (`d` 15 3 2026) (`d` 15 3 2027) FALSE EQUALS `yes: my application is within 12 months (s 198(1), (3))`
#ASSERT `Can I have my costs assessed` `individual` `instructed` `the client` TRUE `no dispute` (`d` 15 3 2026) (`d` 16 3 2027) FALSE EQUALS `no: it is more than 12 months late and the Supreme Court has not determined that it is just and fair to deal with it (s 198(3), (4))`
#ASSERT `Can I have my costs assessed` `individual` `instructed` `a third party payer who owes the costs to the client or someone else` TRUE `no dispute` (`d` 15 3 2026) (`d` 16 3 2027) TRUE EQUALS `yes, though late: the Supreme Court has determined that it is just and fair for it to be dealt with (s 198(4))`
#ASSERT `Can I have my costs assessed` `individual` `instructed` `the client` TRUE `the Commissioner could not resolve the costs dispute and told the parties they may apply for a costs assessment` (`d` 15 3 2026) (`d` 1 9 2026) FALSE EQUALS `yes: my application is within 12 months (s 198(1), (3))`
#ASSERT `Can I have my costs assessed` `individual` `instructed` `the client` TRUE `the costs dispute was resolved, determined by the Commissioner, or is still being dealt with` (`d` 15 3 2026) (`d` 1 9 2026) FALSE EQUALS `no: the costs are or were the subject of a costs dispute before the Commissioner that was not left unresolved with notice of my right to an assessment (s 197)`
#ASSERT `Can I have my costs assessed` `individual` `instructed` `the client` TRUE `VCAT determined the costs dispute under the Victorian Act s 99` (`d` 15 3 2026) (`d` 1 9 2026) FALSE EQUALS `no: VCAT determined the costs dispute (Victorian Act s 99(9))`
#ASSERT `Can I have my costs assessed` `individual` `instructed` `the client` TRUE `the Commissioner arranged a costs assessment under s 284` (`d` 15 3 2020) (`d` 1 9 2026) FALSE EQUALS `the Commissioner's own assessment: the costs are being assessed under s 284, outside any time limit (ss 197(b), 284(2))`
#ASSERT `Can I have my costs assessed` `individual` `instructed` `the client` FALSE `no dispute` (`d` 15 3 2026) (`d` 1 9 2026) FALSE EQUALS `no: Division 7 applies only to costs payable to my own law practice on a solicitor-client basis, not costs ordered to be paid to another party (s 196)`
#ASSERT `Can I have my costs assessed` `government` `instructed` `the client` TRUE `no dispute` (`d` 15 3 2026) (`d` 1 9 2026) FALSE EQUALS `not covered: Part 4.3 does not protect me (s 170, Sch 4 cl 18)`
#ASSERT `What is the last day to apply for a costs assessment` (`d` 31 1 2026) EQUALS `d` 31 1 2027
#ASSERT `What is the last day to apply for a costs assessment` (`d` 29 2 2028) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2029

§§ `s 204 -- who pays for the assessment`

`the practice pays` MEANS `my law practice pays the costs of the costs assessment (s 204(2))`
`the assessor decides` MEANS `the costs assessor decides who pays the costs of the costs assessment (s 204(1))`
-- Claimed $10 000: a cut to $8 500 is exactly 15%; to $8 501 is less.
#ASSERT `Who pays for my costs assessment` 10000 8500 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the practice pays`
#ASSERT `Who pays for my costs assessment` 10000 8501 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the assessor decides`
#ASSERT `Who pays for my costs assessment` 10000 10000 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the practice pays`
#ASSERT `Who pays for my costs assessment` 10000 5000 TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the assessor decides`

§§ `s 272 -- time for a costs complaint`

-- Payable 1 May 2026: 60 days after is 30 June. Itemised bill given 10 June: 30 days after is 10 July.
#ASSERT `What is the last day to complain about my costs` (`d` 1 5 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) EQUALS `d` 30 6 2026
#ASSERT `What is the last day to complain about my costs` (`d` 1 5 2026) TRUE (`d` 10 6 2026) EQUALS `d` 10 7 2026
`in time` MEANS `in time: made within the required period (s 272(2), (3))`
`can be waived` MEANS `late, and the time limit can still be waived if the Commissioner is satisfied that it is just and fair to deal with it (s 272(2))`
`waived` MEANS `late, but the time limit can be and has been waived: within 4 months after the required period, the Commissioner is satisfied it is just and fair, and the law practice has not started proceedings for the costs (s 272(2))`
`too late` MEANS `too late for a costs dispute: the time limit cannot be waived (s 272(2)); the conduct may still be complained of as a disciplinary matter within 3 years (s 272(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my costs complaint in time` `individual` (`d` 1 5 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 30 6 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `Is my costs complaint in time` `individual` (`d` 1 5 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 7 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `can be waived`
#ASSERT `Is my costs complaint in time` `individual` (`d` 1 5 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 30 10 2026) FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `waived`
#ASSERT `Is my costs complaint in time` `individual` (`d` 1 5 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 31 10 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `too late`
#ASSERT `Is my costs complaint in time` `individual` (`d` 1 5 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 7 2026) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `too late`
#ASSERT `Is my costs complaint in time` `individual` (`d` 1 5 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 7 2026) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `too late`
#ASSERT `Is my costs complaint in time` `individual` (`d` 1 5 2026) TRUE (`d` 10 6 2026) (`d` 10 7 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `Is my costs complaint in time` `a law practice` (`d` 1 5 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 6 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no relief as a costs dispute: a commercial or government client cannot obtain relief on a consumer matter (s 268(3))`

§§ `ss 291-294 -- the Commissioner and costs disputes`

#ASSERT `Can the Commissioner deal with my costs dispute` `individual` 99999 50000 EQUALS `yes: the total bill is less than $100 000 (s 291(1)(a))`
#ASSERT `Can the Commissioner deal with my costs dispute` `individual` 100000 9999 EQUALS `yes: the total bill is $100 000 or more, but less than $10 000 is in dispute (s 291(1)(b))`
#ASSERT `Can the Commissioner deal with my costs dispute` `individual` 100000 10000 EQUALS `no: the Commissioner must instead tell me of my right to a costs assessment or to apply to VCAT (s 291(2))`
#ASSERT `Can the Commissioner deal with my costs dispute` `government` 5000 1000 EQUALS `no relief as a costs dispute: a commercial or government client cannot obtain relief on a consumer matter (s 268(3))`

#ASSERT `What happens to my unresolved costs dispute` `individual` 50000 12000 9999 FALSE EQUALS `the Commissioner may make a binding determination of the amount payable, less than $10 000 (s 292); or may notify in writing that it cannot resolve the dispute, and then must tell me of my right to a costs assessment or to VCAT (s 293(2)(b)(ii))`
#ASSERT `What happens to my unresolved costs dispute` `individual` 50000 12000 10000 FALSE EQUALS `the Commissioner must stop and tell me of my right to a costs assessment or to apply to VCAT: $10 000 or more is still in dispute (s 293(2)(b)(i))`
#ASSERT `What happens to my unresolved costs dispute` `individual` 50000 12000 9999 TRUE EQUALS `the Commissioner has notified that it cannot resolve the dispute: it must stop and tell me of my right to a costs assessment or to apply to VCAT (s 293(2)(b)(ii))`
#ASSERT `What happens to my unresolved costs dispute` `individual` 150000 20000 5000 FALSE EQUALS `not covered: the Commissioner cannot deal with this costs dispute (ss 268(3), 291)`
#ASSERT `What happens to my unresolved costs dispute` `government` 50000 12000 5000 FALSE EQUALS `not covered: the Commissioner cannot deal with this costs dispute (ss 268(3), 291)`

§§ `Victorian Act s 99 -- VCAT`

-- Informed 1 August 2026: 60 days after is 30 September.
#ASSERT `Can I take my costs dispute to VCAT` 25000 TRUE (`d` 1 8 2026) (`d` 30 9 2026) EQUALS `yes: I can apply to VCAT, which can order an amount payable of up to $25 000 (Victorian Act s 99(1), (2), (4))`
#ASSERT `Can I take my costs dispute to VCAT` 25000 TRUE (`d` 1 8 2026) (`d` 1 10 2026) EQUALS `no: my application is not within 60 days after the Commissioner informed me (Victorian Act s 99(2))`
#ASSERT `Can I take my costs dispute to VCAT` 25001 TRUE (`d` 1 8 2026) (`d` 2 8 2026) EQUALS `no: more than $25 000 is in dispute (Victorian Act s 99(1)(a))`
#ASSERT `Can I take my costs dispute to VCAT` 5000 FALSE (`d` 1 8 2026) (`d` 2 8 2026) EQUALS `no: the Commissioner has not informed me of my right to apply to VCAT under s 291(2) or s 293(1) (Victorian Act s 99(1)(b))`
